    {
      "slug": "gram:n3-donna-ni-koto-ka",
      "variants": [],
      "nuance_tags": [
        "emphasis"
      ],
      "usage_contexts": [
        "written",
        "literary",
        "spoken"
      ],
      "steps_unavailable": "Pre-predicate adverb plus a fixed closing frame: どんなに opens the clause, the predicate goes in plain form and ことか closes it (どんなに疲れたことか). The closed op enum has no prepend operation, so an ordered sequence from a single base could only emit 疲れたことか and would silently drop the obligatory どんなに slot that the record makes the head of the pattern."
    },
    {
      "slug": "gram:n3-donna-ni-temo",
      "variants": [],
      "nuance_tags": [
        "concession",
        "emphasis"
      ],
      "usage_contexts": [
        "spoken",
        "written"
      ],
      "steps_unavailable": "Pre-predicate adverb plus a concessive tail (どんなに + て-form + も; い-adjective くて + も; な-adjective + でも). With no prepend op any sequence would emit the tail alone — 書いても, 高くても, 静かでも — which is the plain ても concessive, a separate point; the record's whole contrast with どんなに～ことか rests on the どんなに that the steps cannot produce."
    },
